      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about just embedding this data directly as child on the sensor?\n\nI\u0027m not sure of the value of creating a separate node that collects up all the body detect parameters.\n\n```\nbase_accel: base-accel {\n\t\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,lis2dw12\";\n\t\t\tstatus \u003d \"okay\";\n\n\t\t\tactive-mask \u003d \"SENSOR_ACTIVE_S0_S3\";\n\t\t\tlocation \u003d \"MOTIONSENSE_LOC_BASE\";\n\t\t\tmutex \u003d \u003c\u0026mutex_lis2dw12\u003e;\n\t\t\tport \u003d \u003c\u0026i2c_sensor\u003e;\n\t\t\trot-standard-ref \u003d \u003c\u0026base_rot_ref\u003e;\n\t\t\tdefault-range \u003d \u003c2\u003e;\n\t\t\tdrv-data \u003d \u003c\u0026lis2dw12_data\u003e;\n\t\t\ti2c-spi-addr-flags \u003d \"LIS2DWL_ADDR1_FLAGS\";\n\t\t\tbodydetect {\n\t\t\t\tcompatible \u003d \"cros-ec,motionsense-bodydetect\";\n\t\t\t\tvar_noise_factor \u003d \u003c150\u003e;\n\t\t\t\tvar_threshold \u003d \u003c3000\u003e;\n\t\t\t\tconfidence_delta \u003d \u003c2900\u003e;\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t\tconfigs {\n\t\t\t\tcompatible \u003d\n\t\t\t\t\t\"cros-ec,motionsense-sensor-config\";\n\t\t\t\t/* 50 Hz to support body detection. */\n\t\t\t\tec-s0 {\n\t\t\t\t\todr \u003d \u003c(50000 | ROUND_UP_FLAG)\u003e;\n\t\t\t\t};\n\t\t\t\tec-s3 {\n\t\t\t\t\todr \u003d \u003c(50000 | ROUND_UP_FLAG)\u003e;\n\t\t\t\t};\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t};\n```\n\nI think you can still keep `bd_params` as a pointer in the shared motionsense structure.  This just requires using using `DT_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY(cros_ec_motionsense_bodydetect, fn)` to create the `struct body_detect_params` entries.",
